  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "dan-9-24",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Seventy weeks are determined upon your people and your holy city, to finish the transgression, to make an end of sins, to make reconciliation for iniquity, to bring in everlasting righteousness, to seal up vision and prophecy, and to anoint the Most Holy. Textual proof: the window includes Messiah's mission (v25-27); Hebrews 9:26 speaks of Christ appearing at the end of the ages to put away sin by Himself.",
      "density": 4.1821,
      "words": 69,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 43,
      "gate": "FAIL",
      "violations": [
        "43 words (max 35): \"Seventy weeks are determined upon your people and your holy city, to finish the transgress…\""
      ],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Hebrews 9:26"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-12-4",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The book is sealed until the time of the end, when knowledge runs to and fro. First principle: prophecy has a shelf-life of obscurity — the seal opens when the world is ready to run with it.",
      "density": 2.125,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-10-21",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Gabriel will show what is written in the true record; Michael stands as your prince. First principle: history is written down before it happens — the scripture of truth is the script empires must play out.",
      "density": 2.1,
      "words": 36,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-9-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "He shall confirm a covenant with many for one week; in the midst he causes sacrifice and oblation to cease. First principle: Messiah's death ends the efficacy of the old sacrificial system (Heb 10).",
      "density": 1.9929,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-11-31",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Arms pollute the sanctuary and end the daily sacrifice — the desecration Jesus tells readers to watch for. First principle: Daniel 11 is Matthew 24's source text; the abomination is scheduled, and flight is commanded.",
      "density": 1.9036,
      "words": 35,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-10-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Behind the curtain of empires, princes contend — Michael comes to help. First principle: prayer on earth touches war in heaven; the delay of answers is not the absence of angels.",
      "density": 1.8607,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-12-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Michael stands up; unparalleled trouble comes; everyone written in the book is delivered. First principle: the worst time in history has a register of names — deliverance is written, not random.",
      "density": 1.8036,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-12-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "A beatitude attaches to those who endure to the thousand three hundred and five and thirty days. First principle: waiting is blessedness when the timeline is God's — endurance has a numbered horizon.",
      "density": 1.7964,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-9-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "After sixty-two weeks Messiah is cut off, but not for Himself. First principle: the Anointed One dies not for His own sin but for others — Isaiah 53 confirmed.",
      "density": 1.7536,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-12-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Many who sleep in the dust shall awake: some to everlasting life, some to shame. Jesus and Paul and Revelation all cite bodily resurrection. First principle: death is not final; resurrection is universal and decisive.",
      "density": 1.7321,
      "words": 35,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-12-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The oath-sworn duration: when the scattering of the holy people's power is accomplished, all is finished. First principle: the man in linen swears the end of persecution — three-and-a-half times, then done.",
      "density": 1.7143,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-12-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Daniel is dismissed to rest and to rise for his portion at the end of days. First principle: the faithful die with a reserved lot — rest now, standing at the end.",
      "density": 1.7143,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-10-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The glorious man by the river — beryl body, fiery eyes, brass feet, multitude voice. First principle: theophany before the apocalypse: the messenger's glory certifies the message's weight.",
      "density": 1.5571,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-12-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The abomination's setup begins a counted span. First principle: God numbers the desolation — day counts mean the horror has measurable, curfew-able bounds.",
      "density": 1.4893,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-9-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "From the decree to restore Jerusalem until Messiah the Prince. First principle: Daniel dates the coming of the Anointed One within a calculable window.",
      "density": 1.4,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
